From 3dfee59c2cf43d1f93c0b2122ffddd09f13232ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "R. Daneel Olivaw" <rdaneel@gozala.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:44:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(query)!: notation/analyze takes a document's forms,
 and says which each row is about

The input cell is `forms`, a list of the trees notation/read gives, so
an analysis sees the forms beside the one it judges; each row's `at` is
its form's place in the list. supply_read and supply_analyze are hidden
from the docs, for dialog's own crates alone.
